  <sector code="12181" percentage="30" vocabulary="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Healthcare workers in all government facilities in 8 districts will receive training through a cascade model. The devices are provided to the facilities, alongside the training package. The Ministry of Health and Sanitation have been consulted throughout the process to ensure the project is in line with the needs of the health system and is not duplicating efforts. The training will also be extended to the midwifery and Maternal and Child Health (MCH) Aide schools so newly qualified midwives and MCH Aides will have been trained in its use. The Ministry are also encouraging extending the training to final year medical students.</narrative>
  </sector>
  <sector code="12261" percentage="20" vocabulary="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Part of the project targets the communication of the results from the CRADLE VSA to the patients in an attempt to involve patients in their care, engage them in their management and increase the quality of care.</narrative>
  </sector>
  <sector code="12191" percentage="20" vocabulary="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The blood pressure and heart rate monitoring device, which was designed in line with the WHO requirements for a device that is suitable for low resource settings will be provided to all government facilities across 8 of Sierra Leone&apos;s 16 districts in the Phase 1 of this rollout, contributing to medical services.</narrative>
  </sector>
  <sector code="13020" percentage="30" vocabulary="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project focuses on delivering care to women in pregnancy through the use of the CRADLE VSA to detect abnormalities in blood pressure and heart rate and recommends appropriate tailored action in the event of an abnormal result.</narrative>
  </sector>
